  "source": "[\\rational.cauchy.sequence.inv{A ::= a(n_)}]\nDefines: C ::= c(n_) is \\cauchy.rational.sequence\nwhen: A is \\(nonzero)::cauchy.rational.sequence\nexpresses: c(n_) := \\rational.inv(a(n_))\nDocumented:\n. called: \"termwise reciprocal of $A?$\"\n. description: \"For a nonzero Cauchy-real class, its representative is\n                eventually bounded away from zero, so termwise reciprocal gives\n                another Cauchy sequence. Finitely many zero terms are sent to\n                zero by the totalized rational reciprocal.\"\nId: \"9b4a6a46-43f6-41b2-9bac-bffb8fc6dcce\"",
